# Runtime library indices: local observation data, not shipped seed data.
# Built lazily on first write by the CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS schemas in
# each disk_interface, so a fresh clone builds its own; the separate
# verify_and_upgrade_database() only migrates an index that already
# exists, and no-ops when absent. The static bright-star catalog
# (wayfindinglib/drivers/catalog/bright_star_catalog.sqlite) is a bundled
# data asset and stays tracked.
# astrometrics_log.db mutates its own bytes on every Python import (logger
# setup touches it via get_configuration()), so it can never stay
# byte-identical across a pre-commit stash/restore cycle.
# astrometrics.db was tracked as "seed data" until the repository was
# opened up; it is in fact a personal observing log (real targets, capture
# timestamps, and absolute paths into the machine that captured them), so
# it ships with nobody. libraryIndex/.gitkeep keeps the directory itself
# present, which get_library_path() requires -- unlike its wayfindinglib
# counterpart it does not mkdir what it resolves.
astrometricslib/libraryIndex/astrometrics.db
astrometricslib/libraryIndex/astrometrics_log.db
wayfindinglib/libraryIndex/*.db
# Gaia cone-search cache. Regenerated on demand by star_identifier.py, and
# its cached_regions rows encode the sky coordinates actually pointed at,
# so a populated cache is local history rather than a shipped asset.
astrometricslib/libraryIndex/catalogs/catalog_cache.db
# Device and catalog-merge lock files: zero-byte runtime artifacts that
# file_lock() recreates, having first makedirs'd its own parent directory.
astrometricslib/libraryIndex/locks/
# Local calibration-frame index: absolute paths into whichever machine
# captured the darks/flats/biases, so it is meaningless in another clone.
# CalibrationLibrary.load_library() treats a missing file as an empty
# library and save_library() writes a fresh one.
astrometricslib/libraryIndex/calibration_frames.json
# Local configuration: machine-specific frames_path plus the astrometry.net
# API key. Seeded from astrometrics.config.example by setup_venv.sh.
astrometricslib/astrometrics.config
# MCP client config: absolute interpreter paths, per-clone. See
# mcp_servers.example.json.
mcp_servers.json
# Agent local overrides (the ".local." convention is per-machine by design).
.agent/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json
# Scheduler lock: holds a live session id and pid, rewritten every run.
.agent/scheduled_tasks.lock
logs/
.ruff_cache/


